Net sign per `RULES_context_geometry_simulation_2026-08-30.md` §3 criterion 5: shading (added by `EU-16` T06)
lowers solar gain (heating **up**); adiabatic party walls (`EU-16` T07) remove a loss path (heating
**down**); `EU-15`'s carved circulation cores (T05) add unconditioned floor area inside the same footprint,
which does not act in a single predictable direction on the *pooled per-m²* EUI. **These three effects were
not run as a controlled ablation (shading-only / adiabatic-only / cores-only) — this harvest cannot isolate
which one dominates the net move in any district, and none is fabricated here.** Madrid/Lyon/London all moved
**down** (net); Bologna moved **up** (net) — the sign is not uniform across districts, consistent with the
rule's own statement that the net is not predictable in advance. No verdict above authorises any change to a
harvested figure — DR12–16 are external checks against published literature, not a correction applied to the
manifests or `RESULTS_EU-11.md` numbers above.
